---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { ArrowRight, Sparkles, CheckCircle2 } from 'lucide-react';

const title = 'PPMI & Information Content — MoroAI Architecture';
const description = 'Mathematical formulation of Positive Pointwise Mutual Information and Resnik Information Content in MoroAI.';
---

<DocsLayout title={title} description={description} currentSlug="/docs/concepts/ppci-filtering/">
  <div class="not-prose mb-8">
    <span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-moro-400 uppercase tracking-wider bg-moro-500/10 px-2.5 py-1 rounded border border-moro-500/20 mb-3 inline-block">
      Theory & Math
    </span>
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-white tracking-tight">PPMI & Information Content</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-400 text-base mt-2">
      Quantifying semantic domain specificity and conceptual rarity in training datasets.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>1. Positive Pointwise Mutual Information (PPMI)</h2>
  <p>
    Pointwise Mutual Information measures the statistical dependency between a vocabulary token $w$ and the enterprise domain corpus $D$:
  </p>

  <pre class="bg-dark-950 p-4 rounded-xl border border-dark-800 font-mono text-sm text-sky-300">
{`PPMI(w, D) = max(0, log2( P(w | D) / P(w | GeneralCorpus) ))`}
  </pre>

  <p>
    Tokens with high PPMI scores represent high-value domain vocabulary (e.g. <code>pharmacokinetics</code>, <code>depreciation</code>, <code>indemnification</code>). Tokens with zero PPMI represent generic English stop words.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Resnik Information Content</h2>
  <p>
    Concept specificity is measured through Resnik's formulation of Information Content (IC):
  </p>

  <pre class="bg-dark-950 p-4 rounded-xl border border-dark-800 font-mono text-sm text-sky-300">
{`IC(c) = -log2( P(c) )`}
  </pre>

  <p>
    Rare concepts possess high Information Content. Samples with high average IC contain the dense reasoning steps that fine-tuning requires.
  </p>

  <h2>3. k-NN Embedding Density</h2>
  <p>
    To verify whether a sample sits in the dense interior of the training distribution or on its perimeter, MoroAI computes the mean cosine similarity to its $k$-nearest semantic neighbors:
  </p>

  <pre class="bg-dark-950 p-4 rounded-xl border border-dark-800 font-mono text-sm text-sky-300">
{`Density(x_i) = (1 / k) * sum_{j in KNN(x_i)} CosineSimilarity(v_i, v_j)`}
  </pre>

  <div class="not-prose mt-12 pt-6 border-t border-dark-800 flex items-center justify-between">
    <a href="/docs/concepts/data-compiler/" class="text-xs font-semibold text-gray-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">
      ← Epistemic Data Compiler
    </a>
    <a href="/docs/concepts/lineage-graphs/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl bg-moro-500 hover:bg-moro-400 text-white font-semibold text-xs transition-colors">
      <span>Lineage Graphs</span>
      <ArrowRight class="w-3.5 h-3.5" />
    </a>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
